<!-- ============ 12. RISKS ============ -->
<div class="chapter"></div>
<div class="label kicker">11 &middot; Honest caveats</div>
<h2 class="ch">What could go wrong, and what we could not verify</h2>
<table class="t keep">
  <tr><th style="width:30%">Risk</th><th>Mitigation</th></tr>
  <tr><td>PKR tickets are small next to USD work</td><td>Productise: the same WhatsApp agent, site template and reminder engine across every client in a sector. Target 3 to 4 days of team time per Growth build. Quetta wins double as Pakistan SMB case studies.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Shutdowns and lockdowns</td><td>SMS fallback, broadband hosting, offline POS; WhatsApp follow-ups on days you cannot visit.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Owners fear tax exposure</td><td>Never lead with compliance. Offer compliant POS through partners only when the owner raises it.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>No local proof yet</td><td>Founding-client pilots, a live demo, and a public Upwork record. First measured result by week 10.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Meta raises WhatsApp prices again</td><td>Bill messages at cost, keep Starter on the free WhatsApp Business app, keep SMS as a fallback channel.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>A competitor copies the pitch</td><td>They can copy words, not a working demo and a record. Move fast in the beachheads and lock in referrals.</td></tr>
</table>
